 the latest season of  stranger things and we can't wait to see  them all shine on the screen  until the first batch of season 4  episodes arrive events and storylines  remain up for debate that said the  official synopsis has been unveiled by  netflix and audiences are in for a real  treat according to netflix it's been six  months since the battle of star courts  which brought terror and destruction to  hawkins struggling with the aftermath  our group of friends are separated for  the first time and navigating the  complexities of high school hasn't made  things any easier in this most  vulnerable time a new and horrifying  supernatural threat surfaces presenting  a gruesome mystery that if solved might  finally put an end to the horrors of the  upside down as more seasoned audience  members can probably recall high school  comes with its own batch of trials and  tribulations so it'll be interesting to  see how the characters handle life in  the big leagues while dealing with the  madness of the upside down season 3  ended with what looked like hopper and  billy's deaths these events led to joyce  will jonathan and eleven packing their  bags and leaving behind the tainted  memories of hawkins eleven also seems to  have lost her powers to boots what will  then fold remains anyone's guess but if  the synopsis is any indication fans will  be in store for a wild ride in another  horror-like setting what's not to love  about that  look like a million bucks yeah and  you're gonna slam dead like a lion  in an interview on the podcast present  company with christa smith the duffer  brothers hinted at a darker horror movie  vibe for season four if that were even  possible given the events of season  three ross duffer explained how the  series had evolved over the previous  seasons stating when we pitched it to  netflix all those years ago we pitched  it as the kids are the goonies in e.t  that's their storyline that depiction  was initially in contrast to the  atmosphere that older characters  encountered ross continued the adults  are in jaws and close encounters and  then the teens are in nightmare on elm  street or halloween but this year we  don't have the kids we can't do the  goonies anymore and so suddenly we're  leaning much harder into the horror  movie territory that we love now that  the kids are grown up at least in real  life that is gravitating towards the  horror elements of the series sounds  like a delightfully sinister idea  creating a tv series especially one  revolving around child actors isn't easy  that really rings true and the show  isn't only intended for younger  audiences not only did this factor make  it difficult to get stranger things  greenlit but it also meant that the  child actors at the center of their  story would inevitably age out of their  roles this aspect can at times be  painfully obvious suffice it to say the  children actors on stranger things are  no longer kids in a 2017 interview with  the hollywood reporter creators matt and  ross duffer were asked if the kids  ageing put pressure on them to work at a  certain pace ross said it's better to  adjust the narrative to fit the ages  than to try to rush the process  matt added that even if i had the choice  to freeze them in time i wouldn't we  don't want to be repeating ourselves  this show is going to naturally evolve  and feel different year to year and that  to me is a good thing  jim hopper is a complicated character  who quickly became a fan favorite in  season one he's a hero of the town and  in a way a father figure to not just the  children of the series but the  townspeople as well however if the  season 3 finale is any indication the  fictional town won't have its rock for  the foreseeable future as he appeared to  have met his demise luckily appearances  can be deceiving as hopper has already  been shown in a trailer for the upcoming  season alive with a shaved head and in  russia if hopper has a pulse he's likely  going to cause 